From 7c197b9ff7108dfd0eccda95e37d0cb63838e5f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 04:25:26 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 203/258] fix(perf): fold the C6 harness preflight +
 dispatch-overhead fix back onto the R6 tip

Integration cherry-picked the C6 fix 60b9f9b86 (= work-branch c6a97dc80)
before the feature commit e4a61df8b, so the later commit rewrote
scripts/perf/c6_timing_harness.py with the pre-fix version.  Two things
were lost:

  * dispatch_overhead no longer received the TimingProxy and called
    runtime_proxy.collect(); proxy_runtime is a CudaRuntime, which has no
    collect(), so every dispatch round raised AttributeError and was
    swallowed by the per-case try/except into an error dict;
  * the five-sample nvidia-smi preflight window with the
    --preflight-max-utilization-pct abort (and --skip-preflight) was gone,
    so a busy shared GamePC could silently produce a void round.

This commit re-applies the c6a97dc80 delta and preserves the R6 change
(count = m * int(CUDA_W8A8_BLOCK)) that the feature commit carried.
